## 🧠 Learned

### Terminal (macOS / zsh)

| Command | What it does |
|---|---|
| `pwd` | Show the current folder |
| `ls` / `ls -la` | List files (including hidden ones) |
| `cd folder` / `cd ..` | Enter a folder / go up one level |
| `mkdir name` | Create a folder |
| `touch file` | Create an empty file |
| `cat file` | Print a file's contents |
| `mv old new` | Rename or move a file |
| `echo "x" > file` | Write to a file (replaces content) |
| `echo "x" >> file` | Append to a file |

### Git setup

```bash
git config --global user.name "Armand"
git config --global user.email "<id>+<username>@users.noreply.github.com"
git config --global init.defaultBranch main
```

- GitHub's **no-reply email** keeps my real address private
- GitHub needs a **personal access token** instead of a password in the terminal

